= Internet protocol suite — Technical =

The suite follows layered service relationships rather than a rigid software decomposition. IP provides best-effort datagram delivery across networks; transport protocols add end-to-end communication properties; application protocols define service-specific semantics.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* Internet protocol suite ≠ Internet itself
* TCP/IP ≠ TCP and IP only
* protocol layer ≠ implementation layer

== References ==
* IETF RFC 1122, ''Requirements for Internet Hosts — Communication Layers'' (1989).
* IETF RFC 1123, ''Requirements for Internet Hosts — Application and Support'' (1989).
* IETF RFC 8200, ''Internet Protocol, Version 6 (IPv6) Specification'' (2017).
